Vectrix Attribution Notice
==========================

Vectrix is an MIT-licensed rendering-first math library.

This codebase contains:

1) Work derived from JOML
-------------------------
Portions of the library are derived from, adapted from, or based on JOML
(Java OpenGL Math Library), also licensed under MIT.

Primary derived areas include:
- Core vector/matrix/quaternion primitives and related interfaces in `org.dynamisengine.vectrix.core`
- Legacy/compatibility sampling components in `org.dynamisengine.vectrix.sampling`
- Various geometry/intersection utilities and tests that retain JOML lineage

Original JOML copyright notices are preserved in file headers where applicable.

JOML project:
- https://github.com/JOML-CI/JOML

2) Original Vectrix work
------------------------
Substantial portions are original Vectrix implementations, including but not limited to:
- Curve framework (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.curve`)
- FFT and convolution (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.fft`)
- Optics/material math (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.optics`)
- Spherical harmonics (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.sh`)
- LTC evaluation (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.ltc`)
- Rendering math LUT builders (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.renderingmath`)
- GPU packing/compression utilities (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.gpu`)
- SoA and affine kernels (`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.soa`, `org.dynamisengine.vectrix.affine`)
- Hash, easing, SDF, and release-oriented infrastructure additions

3) Third-party data: CIE colorimetric tables (CC BY-SA 4.0)
-----------------------------------------------------------
`org.dynamisengine.vectrix.color.CieData` contains the CIE 1931 and CIE 1964 standard colorimetric observers and
CIE standard illuminant D65 at 1 nm, (c) International Commission on Illumination (CIE), from the CIE open-access
datasets:
- CIE_xyz_1931_2deg.csv, DOI 10.25039/CIE.DS.xvudnb9b
- CIE_xyz_1964_10deg.csv, DOI 10.25039/CIE.DS.sqksu2n5
- CIE_std_illum_D65.csv, DOI 10.25039/CIE.DS.hjfjmt59

licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Changes: reformatted into Java arrays, values unaltered; the
CIE 1964 z-bar-10 entries left undefined (NaN) by the dataset from 560 nm are stored as 0, as tabulated in CIE 15.
That file, and adaptations of it, are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.

